From d62797ac6242c1273b9e120362bb5ec876b83a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:51:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] [conversion] legalize the storage of scalable vectors
 with the patterns alone

On a target with SVE the pipeline ran MLIR's
`arm-sve-legalize-vector-storage` on every function. The cause of the
failure is in that MLIR pass: it applies its patterns with the greedy
driver's default configuration, which also folds and simplifies the
regions of the function, and it fails when the driver has not reached a
fixpoint after ten iterations. Dropping the redundant arguments of a
chain of blocks takes one iteration per block when the blocks are laid
out last first, so a large function without any vector made the whole
compilation fail with `RunPass` and no diagnostic. The pass has no
option for the driver's configuration; no LLVM report has been filed.

`reussir-legalize-vector-storage` applies the same patterns with
folding, constant CSE and region simplification off, and like MLIR's
pass it fails, with a diagnostic, when a use of a legalized allocation
is left that the patterns cannot rewrite. The pipeline and the vector
lowering test use it.
